From 4ca60f75ddc1cfeb22269de01bebeb4d87ab92a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Edward Li <vk.edward.li@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 02:44:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] Emulate reversed-depth viewports on affected AMD Mac
 GPUs

Avoid passing reversed depth ranges directly to Metal on AMD Mac2 GPUs that do not support Metal 3.
For reversed Vulkan viewports, pass Metal a forward depth range by swapping min/max depth, and pass a hidden per-draw viewport mask to vertex/tessellation-evaluation shaders so SPIRV-Cross can emit dynamic clip-space Z inversion.

Disable discarded fragment store checking on the affected path to avoid the helper-thread behavior that breaks OIT rendering.

steamac: backport of KhronosGroup/MoltenVK 74850136 onto utmapp/MoltenVK
geometry-shaders 05604465 (v1.4.1 base). Prerequisite of the
VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable backport (same implicit-buffer/viewport code).
Conflict resolution: keep the fork's SPIRV-Cross pin (the needed SPIRV-Cross
change is carried as a steamac patch), keep the fork's TextureOffset/xfb
implicit buffers and robustness2 options, drop the isNVIDIAGPU()/isIntelGPU()/
isMacGPUFamily1() helpers and the unrelated Mac1 NVIDIA discard-check change
(the fork has no supportsMac1 capability).
